Z||000012||Mach10||10-27-2001||08:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lou:<BR><B>All the electronics for the engine and transmission are self contained on top of the intake manifold.  This means a straight forward positive and negative connection and your done. The engine is smaller than a 350 chevy and 96 pounds lighter .  It will debut on the 2003 model Eldorado ev with 450 hp and will gain 150hp over the coming years. Watch for it at the SEMA show in Vegas as they are already designing after market parts for them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll believe it when I sees it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> No way that it's a simple +/- connection  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Still, you <I>cannot</I> beat a v-12 rumble. Simply can't...<P>Jay: Good to hear it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||artherd||10-28-2001||01:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B><P>Hell, no-one's fixed the N* V-8 YET   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Eh? then what's this sitting in my garage?!  The whole story won't be told untill I get the car rolling (I am doing it right, so it's taking some time) and to a test track for example...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But yeah, the way to solve it all is just to junk that ECU, and go aftermarket engine management from the guys at chrfab.com.  good stuff, comes with a harness.<P>4-cam v8 love. Rowar.<P>Yes, I do want that V12 in a bad way!!!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000014||Pontiaddict||10-28-2001||01:48 AM||||By the time the N* swap is perfected, there's gonna be a new series of N* to deal with.<BR>Like a v8 redesigned to be an 8 cyl version of that v-12 there.<BR>Good luck finding a relatively cheap computer that will handle the VVT and variable intake controls. I doubt that the new computers will be easier to deal with than the current ones.||||reg||1
